Subject: [PATCH 7/9] geph5-misc-rpc: android libc dependency

android_state_dir() (patch 0002) probes the effective uid with
libc::geteuid(). The android target had no direct libc dependency in this
crate, so the probe would not resolve. A target-gated dependency table, the
same shape as the geph5-app one in patch 0001: nothing short of a workspace
restructure can make this conflict.

Deliberately last-but-two: dependency tables are the least fragile patch in
any series, and appending keeps the existing numbering stable.

---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libraries/geph5-misc-rpc/Cargo.toml b/libraries/geph5-misc-rpc/Cargo.toml
index cc4bf27..deb834e 100644
--- a/libraries/geph5-misc-rpc/Cargo.toml
+++ b/libraries/geph5-misc-rpc/Cargo.toml
@@ -31,3 +31,7 @@ socksv5 = "0.3"
 tachyonix = "0.3.1"
 geph5-broker-protocol = { version="0.4.0", path = "../geph5-broker-protocol" }
 sillad-meeklike = {version="0.2.1", path="../sillad-meeklike"}
+
+[target.'cfg(target_os = "android")'.dependencies]
+# euid probe for android_state_dir (root module vs. Termux install).
+libc = "0.2"
